  "verbalization": "Hydrocortisone is shown to have a relationship with Dipeptidyl peptidase IX through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Hydrocortisone acts as a target for several entities, which in turn target Dipeptidyl peptidase IX. Specifically, Hydrocortisone is linked to 11-cis retinol dehydrogenase, which is a target of 5-Alpha-Androstane-3-Beta,17beta-Diol, and subsequently to Dipeptidyl peptidase IX. Another pathway connects Hydrocortisone to 11-cis retinol dehydrogenase, which is also a target of 2-[(4S)-4-hydroxy-3,6-dioxodioxan-4-yl]acetic acid, which also targets Dipeptidyl peptidase IX. Additionally, Hydrocortisone is linked to Kallistatin, which is a target of Androstenediol, which also targets Dipeptidyl peptidase IX. These findings collectively suggest that Hydrocortisone may influence Dipeptidyl peptidase IX through a series of molecular interactions, though the exact nature of these interactions remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence is consistent across multiple pathways, indicating a potential role for Hydrocortisone in modulating Dipeptidyl peptidase IX activity, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct relationship.",
